* P-SSHI DEVICE SWEEP FOR 1.7 V MAX PIEZO, nA/uA CURRENT
*
* Set NPN transistor Value to: {npn}
* Set PNP transistor Value to: {pnp}
* Set swept diode Value to:    {Diode}
*
* Active sweep size: 3 NPN x 3 PNP x 5 diodes = 45 runs.
*
* IMPORTANT:
* - TIP31C/TIP32C and other power BJTs are intentionally excluded.
* - At nA/uA current, leakage, low-current gain and junction capacitance matter
*   more than ampere rating or low high-current on-resistance.
* - Compare harvested load power, startup success and switching timing, not only
*   peak inductor current.

* -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
* NPN CANDIDATES
* -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
* 2N5089: very high nominal gain and low junction capacitance
* BC847C: high-gain small-signal SMD transistor
* 2N3904: common baseline model
.model 1 ako:2N5089
.model 2 ako:BC847C
.model 3 ako:2N3904

* -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
* PNP CANDIDATES
* -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
* 2N5087: low-capacitance small-signal PNP
* BC857C: high-gain small-signal SMD PNP
* 2N3906: common baseline model
.model 4 ako:2N5087
.model 5 ako:BC857C
.model 6 ako:2N3906

* -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
* DIODE CANDIDATES
* -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
* RB751CM-40: low-current, very-low-capacitance Schottky candidate
* BAT54: common low-current Schottky benchmark
* BAS40HY: low-capacitance Schottky benchmark
* MMSD4148: very-low-capacitance silicon diode; lower leakage but higher Vf
* 1N4148: common silicon reference
.model 7  ako:RB751CM-40
.model 8  ako:BAT54
.model 9  ako:BAS40HY
.model 10 ako:MMSD4148
.model 11 ako:1N4148

* -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
* ACTIVE SWEEPS
* -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
.step param npn list 1 2 3
.step param pnp list 4 5 6
.step param Diode list 7 8 9 10 11

